  "title": "The Chain of Screaming",
  "cn": "第 15 集 · 怒吼链",
  "novel": "Marshall's boss Arthur [[screamed|scream]] at everyone. The [[chain|chain]] of screaming went from top to bottom: Arthur screamed at Marshall, Marshall screamed at Ted, Ted screamed at a [[stranger|stranger]].\n\nMarshall decided to [[confront|confront]] Arthur [[directly|directly]]. His heart [[pounded|pound]], his hands [[trembled|tremble]], but he stood his ground. \"You can't talk to me like that,\" he said.\n\nTo his [[shock|shock]], Arthur [[respected|respect]] him for it. \"Finally, someone with [[courage|courage]],\" Arthur [[admitted|admit]]. Marshall had [[earned|earn]] his respect.\n\nBarney [[declared|declare]] that the chain of screaming was natural. \"Everyone [[passes|pass]] it down,\" he [[explained|explain]].\n\nBut Marshall [[refused|refuse]] to pass it on. He [[broke|break]] the chain. \"Someone has to stop it,\" he said.\n\nStanding up to a [[bully|bully]], Marshall [[realized|realize]], required more [[courage|courage]] than screaming back. It required the strength to be [[calm|calm]].",
